<p class="vac-caption">A transaction-count model for a tiny table whose live tuples can all be frozen; no retained horizon prevents progress. The age values are invented. The 200-million marker is a maintenance trigger, not the wraparound limit. Freezing changes visibility metadata, leaving the business value intact.</p>
<details><summary>Figure as text</summary><ol><li>With no dead versions, the table’s frozen boundary is 20 million transactions old.</li><li>Other work consumes 160 million more XIDs. The price is unchanged, but the boundary is now 180 million old.</li><li>Vacuum freezes eligible tuples and advances the table boundary. The page can become all-frozen.</li><li>After another 20 million XIDs, the recorded boundary ages again. The frozen tuple remains safe and the all-frozen page can be skipped.</li></ol></details></figure>
<script>
import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-vac-age]')){
 const q=(s:string)=>root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(s)!;
 stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw:(step:number)=>{
  const values=[20,180,0,20];
  q('[data-age]').textContent=`${values[step]} million`;
  q('[data-age-bar]').style.width=`${values[step]/2}%`;
  q('[data-status]').textContent=step<2?'Live tuple · insertion XID not yet frozen':'Live tuple · insertion XID frozen';
  q('[data-frozen]').textContent=step<2?'No':'Yes';
  q('[data-explanation]').textContent=[
   'The price is live and unchanged. The table’s frozen boundary is already 20 million transactions behind.',
   'Other work consumes 160 million more transaction IDs. P7 has not changed, but the table’s frozen boundary is now 180 million transactions old.',
   'Vacuum freezes eligible live tuples and advances the recorded boundary. Here it reaches the current horizon; the business price stays 22.00.',
   'Another 20 million transaction IDs are consumed. The recorded boundary ages again, but this tuple remains frozen. The all-frozen page need not be scanned again for freezing.'
  ][step];
 }});
}
</script>
